{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the highest-priority uncertainty is whether the image modality adds complementary signal to RNA. config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the most direct extension of config_001: it keeps the RNA encoder and profile setting identical and adds only the image branch with a simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of adding image information with minimal confounds. If accuracy improves meaningfully over 48.5%, it confirms multimodal fusion is worth further exploration (better image encoders, fusion strategies, multiprofile). If it does not improve, it tells me the image modality (at least via resnet50) is not complementary to this RNA representation, redirecting budget toward RNA encoder quality or multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment resolves the most impactful design-axis question (model setting) before committing budget to deeper sub-axes like aggregation or fusion method."
}

